# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Haidi Wang et al. (2025). Uni2D: A Universal Machine Learning Interatomic Potential for Two-Dimensional Materials.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2506.07043  arXiv:2506.07043v3
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2506.07043v3 (sha256 cfd32c543e3331a9...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 406 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/wang2025uni2d.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the Uni2D data set (about 20,000 2D materials from
# C2DB and 2dMatpedia with strain and perturbation augmentation; 327,000
# structure-energy-force-stress mappings; VASP optB88-vdW(+U); 90/5/5),
# the Uni2D model (MatterSim framework on the M3GNet architecture; 200
# epochs) with its stated training-set MAEs, the four seed models on
# 1,685 independent PyXtal structures (Table S2), the E / EF / EFS
# target ablation (Table S1), and the comparison with pretrained bulk
# uMLIPs on about 2,000 2D structures (Table 1). Relaxed areas, lattice
# parameters and screening results are properties.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

