# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Training on one NVIDIA RTX 4090D. DFT and Uni2D single-point times were compared on a 48-core Xeon Gold 6248R node (Fig. S3, figure-only).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Energy MAEs in eV/atom are converted exactly to meV/atom (original values in the locations). Force MAEs are per Cartesian component. Each model in Table 1 is compared with its own DFT level, and the MatterSim, M3GNet and CHGNet versions are not stated, so they are paper-local runs.
# - Test-set MAEs on the random 5 % split are figure-only (Fig. S2). Relaxed-area MAEs and R2 values (Table 1), lattice parameters and stability screening are properties or correlation measures. The Table S1 evaluation set is not stated, so its role is null.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/wang2025uni2d.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

